WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:14.133
Each fictional product attribute has a value and unit for the writer.

2
00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:19.733
The headset's product record brings its battery life and features together.

3
00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:15.133
A catalogue request asks the writer for product copy.

4
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:22.467
Supplier notes bring claims for the workflow to check against product attributes.

5
00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:28.267
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the merchandiser.

6
00:01:28.333 --> 00:02:00.133
Saving the request starts the writing and checking workflow.

7
00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:39.067
The checked draft is ready for the merchandiser's review.

8
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:57.333
The short and long descriptions follow the fictional product's attributes.

9
00:02:57.467 --> 00:03:03.733
Each configured figure and feature points back to its product attribute.

10
00:03:03.867 --> 00:03:11.333
The checks identify supplier claims that need correction.

11
00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:44.467
The workflow view shows the writing and checking steps together.

12
00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:37.267
An automated test adds the merchandiser's decision for this product.

13
00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:43.133
The decision names the exact text version being approved.

14
00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:49.667
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the merchandiser.

15
00:04:49.667 --> 00:05:03.533
The workflow rechecks the decision, draft version and current product attributes.

16
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:33.133
The recorded decision is applied to this exact draft version.

17
00:06:28.867 --> 00:06:36.500
The approved text reaches the demo catalogue with its recorded decision.

18
00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:40.980
An automated setup prepares the fictional product's 14-hour battery draft.

19
00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.180
That draft's recorded approval places its text on the demo catalogue.

20
00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:49.380
Another 14-hour draft is ready for review.

21
00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:06.660
The demo catalogue displays the approved 14-hour description.

22
00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:27.500
Typed by Claude (automated test): battery changes to 12 hours.

23
00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:45.340
The waiting draft keeps the 14-hour value used when it was written.

24
00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:53.900
An automated test enters an approval for the older draft.

25
00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:58.940
The decision identifies the exact older text version.

26
00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:15.980
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the merchandiser.

27
00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:23.340
The workflow holds the older draft because its source attributes changed.

28
00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:49.740
A new request asks the writer to use the updated attributes.

29
00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:07.980
The corrected draft says 12 hours and replaces the older waiting draft.

30
00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:26.060
The demo catalogue retains the approved text while the corrected draft waits.

31
00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:28.300
The fictional product's battery value returns to 14 hours.
